<title>USA: U.S. crop condition and progress highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. crop condition and progress highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture on Monday rated 3 percent of the corn crop in very poor condition, 8 percent poor, 28 percent fair, 46 percent good and 15 percent excellent.</p>
<p>The department pegged 3 percent of the soybean crop in very poor condition, 11 percent poor, 33 percent fair, 42 percent good and 11 percent excellent.</p>
<p>The department said 4 pct of the corn crop was harvested, and 20 pct was mature.</p>
<p>USDA pegged 2 percent of the cotton crop in very poor condition, 10 percent poor, 29 percent fair, 46 percent good and 13 percent excellent.</p>
<p>It said 17 percent of the soybean crop was dropping leaves.</p>
<p>USDA said 91 percent of the spring wheat crop had been harvested.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8394</p>
</text>
